Presence of this file opts the project into the protoblast plugin's checkDirectClockReads
compile gate (no Java source, test sources included, may read the wall clock directly --
every current-time read goes through protoblast's offset clock, Now.instant()/Now.millis()
(or Blast.now()/Blast.millis()), so a test can move time without the code caring; the
offset is a constant, so elapsed-time measurement is safe on it too. System.nanoTime() is
not a wall clock and stays allowed; see CheckDirectClockReadsTask).
